<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:core="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:trl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Trials;assembly=OpenRigs.Trials"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:gl="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Shaders;assembly=Bonsai.Shaders"
                 xmlns:ext="clr-namespace:;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:task="clr-namespace:UclOpenCoenDomeDecisionMakingTask;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml, read by ReadLabRig, which publishes it to every device piece; the launch's own, which rig-control always sets to C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs. ExperimentRecords and LiveView take it from ReadLabRig." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <Description>This machine's rig.yml (ConfigRoot\&lt;RIG&gt;\rig.yml) read once into the lab rig model: RigConfigs, RigFile and ConfigRoot, which every device piece reads. First, before anything that reads them.</Description>
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SessionId" Description="The session number; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
        <Property Name="LaunchId" Description="The launcher's run id; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" Description="The mouse's lab ID; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl) over TCP 5561: SubjectId (the mouse's lab ID, or test), SessionId and LaunchId (the launcher's run id, which the manifest records) are the launch's; the experiment declares no parameter of its own: the task's own settings are the task file's, which rig-control writes at launch and again at Go with the form's edits, and names in TaskPath, its curriculum the only record of the stage; the pieces declare their own parameters and commands. The workflow starts into ready mode (devices connected, spouts homed and at this mouse's positions, live view on, nothing recorded) and reports Ready from DomeHardware. LaunchSettings (OpenRigs.Control) publishes SubjectId and TaskPath at Start and ExperimentIds (SubjectId, SessionId) at Go. TaskFile publishes the stage as CurriculumStage (code-version, like S03A-k7f2, from the task file's curriculum) at Go and reports it as the metric curriculumStage. SpoutStepSize and the spout commands are DomeHardware's LickSpoutStage's, which takes the step size live and shows its default. RewardValve-Left.Reward and RewardValve-Right.Reward each give 2.5 ul before and during a run through the valve's calibration (each RewardValve piece's manual drop, a fixed drop).</Description>
        <SubjectId />
        <SessionId />
        <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
        <Parameters />
        <Commands />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="TaskPath" Description="The task file: rig-control's copy of the one chosen at launch, read at Go with the form's edits; from the editor, config\task-localization.yml." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:LaunchSettings.bonsai">
        <SubjectId />
        <TaskPath>..\config\task-localization.yml</TaskPath>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskFile</Name>
        <Description>Reads the task file (TaskPath) at Go, with the form's edits, into TaskText (the file's text, OpenRigs.Core TaskFileText) and TaskConfig, read by ReadTask, which keeps a trial condition's set values as numbers and bools. TaskRules, after ConnectForTaskZapitDaq, checks it at Go and builds the trials' rules.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Core:TaskFileText.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:ReadTask" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Declarations</Name>
        <Description>Subjects the groups share. TrialEvents, the trial loop's events (RunTrials); Trial, each trial at its start; TrialRow, each trial's WorkflowData_Trials row, built at its outcome; GratingAzimuthDeg, the response; StimulusTrial, the trial at its stimulus, for the grating and the sound; StimulusOff, the trial at its StimulusOff event (OpenRigs.Trials StimulusTiming: stimulus.durationSeconds after the stimulus, or stimulus.responseToStimulusOffSeconds after the outcome if sooner), once a trial. Zapit's commands, events and bank (Zapit.Commands, Zapit.Events, Zapit.Bank) are ConnectForTaskZapitDaq's, RewardRequests Rewards'.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="ext:Trial">
              <rx:Name>Trial</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="trl:TrialEvent(ext:Trial,ext:DecisionUpdate,ext:TrialOutcome)">
              <rx:Name>TrialEvents</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(ext:TrialRow)">
              <rx:Name>TrialRow</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Double">
              <rx:Name>GratingAzimuthDeg</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="ext:Trial">
              <rx:Name>StimulusTrial</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="ext:Trial">
              <rx:Name>StimulusOff</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:ExperimentLogs.bonsai">
        <Description>The experiment folder at Go (PathPrefix), WorkflowData_Events, Settings_Rig, Settings_Experiment and the Recording phase. Before DomeHardware: every device's log waits for PathPrefix, so its definition must read nothing the devices define.</Description>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="DisplayDevice" Description="The display the dome projector is on (DomeHardware's ProjectorDisplay); a launch property." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:DomeHardware.bonsai">
        <Description>Every dome device as a piece, named as in the data (lib-open-rigs Building Blocks): the Ready gate, the timestamp generator's clock, the Behavior board with its reward lines, Zapit line and wheel, both Lickety Splits, the lick spout stage, the three cameras, which start triggering once all three acquire, the speakers (SpeakerMixer) and the projector (ProjectorDisplay, stimuli on DrawStimuli). The dome's devices (OpenRigs.Devices DomeHardware: every device as a piece, each logging itself; the cameras triggered once all three acquire; the speakers and their mixer; the projector, DisplayDevice a launch property), with Ready once the Harp clock is set, the spouts are homed, each camera has sent a frame and the mixer has started, and a stop naming what never came after 180 s.</Description>
        <WorkflowStages>LabClockChecked</WorkflowStages>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="LaserCeilingVolts" Description="The laser ceiling as control volts (ConnectForTaskZapitDaq's): rig.yml's zapit.ceilingMw through the rig's laser curve, lib_zapit's max_control_volts, a launch property from rig-control. ZapitDaq and the Zapit setup refuse any laser volts above it; 0, the default, refuses any laser." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ConnectForTaskZapitDaq.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskRules</Name>
        <Description>At Go, CheckTaskAtGo builds the trial conditions from TaskText (each condition's set over the task's values), checks the task once with rig.yml and, in an optogenetics experiment, the Zapit bank the setup loaded (Zapit.Bank, ConnectForTaskZapitDaq's: hence after it), and publishes the trials' rules (TrialRules) for TaskLogic, and the stage as CurriculumStage.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskText</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Zapit.Bank</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>CheckTaskAtGo</Name>
              <Description>The task file's text checked once, at Go, and the trials' rules built from it (TrialRules, tested C#): the task file's curriculum present and well formed, each trial condition built (its set and pairs over the task's values, every combination), rig.yml's speakers, the draw's rules (TrialDraw.CheckTask: a stage past the table, the x-rules, a go/no-go task with no go trials, a laser that would outlast the next trigger, ...) and with optogenetics the Zapit bank the setup loaded (its conditions, its longest ramp-down; none loaded is refused). A problem stops the workflow here, naming each, before the first trial.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CheckTaskAtGo" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>CurriculumStage</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>CurriculumStage</Name>
              <Description>The stage as code-version (S03A-k7f2) from the task file's curriculum, found well formed by CheckTaskAtGo.</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>curriculumStage</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Display</Name>
        <Description>Each trial's grating, drawn on DomeHardware's projector (DrawStimuli).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>StimulusTrial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>ShowGrating</Name>
              <Description>Draws a trial's grating from StimulusTrial until StimulusOff: contrast, elevation and phase the trial's, the rest its combination's, the azimuth the trial's, then GratingAzimuthDeg's as the licks move it (so its first frame is never the last trial's), on for 50 ms at each pulse, every 1/stimulus.rateHz seconds (Flicker), with the photodiode square black on its on frames and white on its off frames.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>DrawStimuli</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Name>Flicker</Name>
                    <Description>Each frame with whether the grating shows: on from each pulse onset (PulseOnsets, every 1/stimulus.rateHz seconds) until 50 ms later (PulseOffsets, as long as the sound's pulse), both on the render clock (Bonsai.Shaders Timer and Delay). A render-clock stimulus, not a task wait.</Description>
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
                    <Name>On?</Name>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Expression>Item2</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
                    <Name>Off?</Name>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Expression>!Item2</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Item1</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Contrast" Selector="visualInitialContrast" />
                      <Property Name="LocationY" Selector="VisualStimulus.InitialElevationDeg" />
                      <Property Name="Phase" Selector="visualPhaseRad" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="TemporalFrequency" Selector="VisualStimulus.InitialTemporalFrequencyHz" />
                      <Property Name="SpatialFrequency" Selector="VisualStimulus.InitialSpatialFrequencyCpd" />
                      <Property Name="Angle" Selector="VisualStimulus.InitialOrientationDeg" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Aperture" Selector="it" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>Aperture</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>The Gaussian window's sigma relative to the grating's 100 degree extent, each trial's (its combination's visualStimulus.initialSigmaDeg).</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>VisualStimulus.InitialSigmaDeg * 2 / 100.0</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="LocationX" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>GratingAzimuthDeg</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawGratings.bonsai">
                    <LocationX>0</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>0</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <ExtentX>100</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>100</ExtentY>
                    <SpatialFrequency>0.06666667</SpatialFrequency>
                    <TemporalFrequency>0</TemporalFrequency>
                    <Phase>0</Phase>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <SquareWave>false</SquareWave>
                    <Contrast>0</Contrast>
                    <DutyCycle xsi:nil="true" />
                    <Radius>1</Radius>
                    <Aperture>0.4</Aperture>
                    <Opacity>1</Opacity>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>StimulusOff</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawQuad.bonsai">
                    <ExtentX>30</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>30</ExtentY>
                    <LocationX>130</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>-22.5</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <ColorR>0</ColorR>
                    <ColorG>0</ColorG>
                    <ColorB>0</ColorB>
                    <ColorA>1</ColorA>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:TakeUntil" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawQuad.bonsai">
                    <ExtentX>30</ExtentX>
                    <ExtentY>30</ExtentY>
                    <LocationX>130</LocationX>
                    <LocationY>-22.5</LocationY>
                    <Layer>0</Layer>
                    <Angle>0</Angle>
                    <ColorR>1</ColorR>
                    <ColorG>1</ColorG>
                    <ColorB>1</ColorB>
                    <ColorA>1</ColorA>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:IgnoreElements" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>PulsePeriod</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>One pulse period, 1/stimulus.rateHz seconds, the trial's.</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>TimeSpan.FromSeconds(1.0 / Stimulus.RateHz)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>VisualTrial</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>gratingAzimuthDeg</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
                    <Name>PulseOnsets</Name>
                    <Description>Each pulse's onset, every 1/stimulus.rateHz seconds from the first frame, on the render clock: a timer made once the trial's period is known (inside SelectMany), as a timer started first would keep its default period.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                          <Name>Source1</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                          <PropertyMappings>
                            <Property Name="Period" />
                          </PropertyMappings>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="gl:Timer">
                            <gl:DueTime>PT0S</gl:DueTime>
                            <gl:Period>PT0.125S</gl:Period>
                          </Combinator>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>true</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Name>PulseOffsets</Name>
                    <Description>Each pulse's end, 50 ms after its onset (AuditoryStimulusSet.PulseSeconds, each sound pulse's length), on the render clock.</Description>
                    <Combinator xsi:type="gl:Delay">
                      <gl:DueTime>PT0.05S</gl:DueTime>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>false</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="12" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="30" To="31" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="17" To="31" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="31" To="16" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="18" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="18" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="18" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="18" Label="Source4" />
                  <Edge From="16" To="18" Label="Source5" />
                  <Edge From="18" To="20" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="23" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="23" To="22" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="19" To="22" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="25" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="25" To="24" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="19" To="24" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="26" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="27" To="28" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="28" To="32" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="34" To="35" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="33" To="36" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="35" To="36" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="36" To="4" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="32" To="33" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="32" To="34" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Audio</Name>
        <Description>The sounds, played by DomeHardware's speakers and mixer (OpenRigs.Audio SpeakerMixer: Speakers, and the mixer started no sooner than 3 s after Start, never sooner, as a fault while the sound card boots can blue-screen the PC); each trial's sound at its auditoryInitialLevelDbfs (the set measured as one, one gain), TaskLogic's penalty sound at each penalised trial's kind's sound.levelDbfs (penalty.incorrect or penalty.noResponse), laid out at Go at the highest level any condition can draw; the background noise at the lab's -60 dBFS, sent at Ready. The auditory stimulus set equalised for rig.yml's speakers at Start (LoadAuditoryStimulusSet into StimulusWaveforms), then at Go for the highest level any condition can draw, each pulse's train at every stimulus.rateHz for the longest stimulus.durationSeconds (TrialRules into LevelAuditoryStimulusSet, into StimulusSoundBuffers, which stops the workflow, naming the condition and speaker, if any would peak at -1 dBFS after equalisation); the lab's penalty sound (PlayPenaltySound, in TaskLogic) on penaltySoundChannel at the penalised kind's sound.levelDbfs. The background noise is the BackgroundNoise include's, after this group.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:LoadAuditoryStimulusSet">
                <ext:Folder>sounds</ext:Folder>
                <ext:FilePrefix>filtered_pink_pulse_</ext:FilePrefix>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>StimulusWaveforms</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>StimulusWaveforms</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:LevelAuditoryStimulusSet" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>StimulusSoundBuffers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>StimulusTrial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>AuditoryTrial?</Name>
              <Description>A trial at auditoryStimulus.initialLevelDbfs mute (auditoryInitialLevelDbfs NaN) plays no sound.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>!double.IsNaN(auditoryInitialLevelDbfs)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>StimulusSoundBuffers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>PlayAuditoryStimulus</Name>
              <Description>Plays a trial's sound: its waveform equalised for its speaker (the channel of rig.yml's speaker nearest the drawn location; at "all" every speaker's channel, each its own copy), at its auditoryInitialLevelDbfs, with the sync copy on rig.yml's syncChannel at syncGain.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:SelectAuditoryStimulus" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>LoopStimulusSounds</Name>
              <Description>The trial's one-period buffer, which the mixer loops from the stimulus (OpenRigs.Audio SpeakerMixer) until StopStimulusSounds.</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>StimulusOff</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>StopStimulusSounds</Name>
              <Description>The stimulus sound stopped with the grating (OpenRigs.Audio SpeakerMixer: faded over 5 ms) at the trial's StimulusOff event: stimulus.durationSeconds after the stimulus, or stimulus.responseToStimulusOffSeconds after the outcome if sooner.</Description>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Audio:BackgroundNoise.bonsai">
        <Description>The background noise, the lab's one file, rig.yml's speakerArray.backgroundNoise (60 s of white noise, 32-bit float), unequalised on every speaker at the lab's -60 dBFS (OpenRigs.Audio SoundLevel.BackgroundDbfs) from Ready.</Description>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Logging</Name>
        <Description>Everything else written to the experiment folder (ExperimentLogs, before DomeHardware, makes it at Go, with WorkflowData_Events, Settings_Rig and Settings_Experiment; each device logs itself): ConditionedTaskLogsZapitDaq (OpenRigs.Logging) writes Settings_Combinations (TrialRules.CombinationsJson) every combination the conditions built at Go, each a row the trial log's trialCombinationId names, with the values that vary, and through TaskLogsZapitDaq Settings_Task (the task file as JSON), WorkflowData_Trials and each ZapitDaq event as an Events row (Event Zapit); the Zapit bank, sample, scanner fit, accuracy and conditions copy are app-rig-control's files, the scanner frames and Camera-Zapit ConnectForTaskZapitDaq's; Rewards (OpenRigs.Devices) logs each reward (RewardDelivered) and each RewardValve piece its calibration file (a valve with no calibration stops the workflow, for every mouse); ExperimentRecords, last but LiveView, adds the controller's events to WorkflowData_Events, records the Harp devices and writes the manifest.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="task:SerializeToJson">
                <task:Formatting>Indented</task:Formatting>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:ConditionedTaskLogsZapitDaq.bonsai" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Status</Name>
        <Description>The current trial's facts as metrics, named as WorkflowData_Trials's columns: the shared trialNumber, trialType, rewardOfferedUl and laserCondition (OpenRigs.Control ReportTrialMetrics), then the task's own target, visualInitialAzimuthDeg and auditoryInitialAzimuthDeg (the curriculumStage, code-version, is TaskFile's); rig-control computes counts, water and performance from the files.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportTrialMetrics">
                <orcl:Members>trialNumber,trialType,rewardOfferedUl,laserCondition</orcl:Members>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>target</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>target</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>visualInitialAzimuthDeg</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>visualInitialAzimuthDeg</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>auditoryInitialAzimuthDeg</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>auditoryInitialAzimuthDeg</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:Rewards.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:RewardValve.bonsai">
        <Name>RewardValve-Left</Name>
        <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
        <BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>
        <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:RewardValve.bonsai">
        <Name>RewardValve-Right</Name>
        <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
        <BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.TriggerCalibratedPulse</BoardTriggerCalibratedPulseSubjectName>
        <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskLogic</Name>
        <Description>The trials, every time on the Harp clock: TrialRules (checked and built at Go, TaskFile's CheckTaskAtGo) run by lib-open-rigs' TrialLoop (RunTrials) into TrialEvents once the experiment folder exists, the first trial's interval starting then; each kind picked from them (PickTrialEvents) and sent to the hardware. Start: Trial (Status) and, at trial 1's, the rules' seed (TrialRules.Seed); Arm and Trigger: ZapitDaq's Arm and the ZapitTrigger line raised, cleared at TriggerOff (OpenRigs.Trials ZapitDaqTrials, given the rules, whose Laser times it); Stimulus: the grating and the sound; Update: the decision variable and the grating's azimuth; StimulusOff (OpenRigs.Trials StimulusTiming: the earlier of stimulus.durationSeconds after the stimulus and stimulus.responseToStimulusOffSeconds after the outcome): the grating hidden and the sound stopped, once a trial; the cues SpoutsIn (spouts.stimulusToSpoutsInSeconds after the stimulus, before it when negative) and SpoutsOut (spouts.rewardConsumptionSeconds into the next interval: the spouts out unless the coming trial's are always in); Outcome: the trial's row (TrialRow), the reward (RewardRequests), the penalty sound and, on the projector, the penalty flash (PlayPenaltyFlash). Every spout move is lib-open-rigs' SpoutCommands' over all the events: trial 1's spouts out at its interval start, the SpoutsIn and SpoutsOut cues', the outcome's. Zapit adds no time.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item1</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>OnNextTick</Name>
              <Description>The rules, once the experiment folder exists, stamped with the next Harp clock tick and given from the clock's thread (lib-open-rigs' OpenRigs.Core OnNextTick): the first trial's interval starts then.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:OnNextTick" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Value</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>WheelDistanceCm</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LickStateLeft</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LickStateRight</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Zapit.Events</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>RunTrials</Name>
              <Description>The trials (TrialRules, tested C#, run by lib-open-rigs' TrialLoop) on the Harp clock: each drawn at its interval's start (the last trial's end, its response window's end whatever the choice, plus its timeout), started at the interval's end less the lead (max(laserToStimulusSeconds, 0)) or later until the quiet waits hold (both spouts released for lickQuietSeconds; the wheel within wheelQuietCm over the last wheelQuietSeconds), the stimulus the lead after the start in every experiment, the response window stimulusToResponseWindowSeconds after it for responseWindowSeconds (each lick 1 left or -1 right on the decision variable, the grating moved azimuthShiftPerLickDeg a lick; left at thresholdLicks, right at -thresholdLicks, else noResponse at the window's end), the outcome, its timeout; with optogenetics each trial armed (Arm), triggered laserToStimulusSeconds before the stimulus unless answered first, and its line cleared laserDurationSeconds later (TriggerOff), the next armed once its whole ZapitDaq trial has played; or with optogenetics.laserEnd stimulusOff the laser early-stopped at the trial's StimulusOff (LaserOff, at most laserDurationSeconds after the trigger: LaserCap), the line cleared and the next armed once ZapitDaq.EarlyStopLeadSeconds (0.1 s), a scan cycle, the ramp-down and a margin have passed. Inputs: the rules, the clock, the wheel, the left and right lick states, ZapitDaq's events (Zapit.Events).</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:RunTrials" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Start</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2.Seed</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogRngSeed.bonsai">
              <Description>The seed every draw of the experiment follows from (the task file's rngSeed, or one drawn at Go when it is null), logged once at trial 1's start.</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialRules</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Trials:ZapitDaqTrials.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Stimulus</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>StimulusTrial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Update</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Update.GratingAzimuthDeg</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>GratingAzimuthDeg</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>StimulusOff</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>StimulusOff</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:PickTrialEvents">
                <trl:Kind>Outcome</trl:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Outcome</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Trials:TrialOutcomeEffects.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Name>SpoutCommands</Name>
              <Description>Every spout move, from the trial events (lib-open-rigs OpenRigs.Trials SpoutCommands): the spouts out at trial 1's interval start and at each SpoutsOut cue, unless the coming trial's spouts are always in (spouts.alwaysIn); at each SpoutsIn cue the trial's own (ISpoutTrial: the target's spout alone on a single-spout trial, singleSpoutOffered, else both in); at the outcome, unless the trial's spouts are always in, the rewarded spout alone, else both out.</Description>
              <Combinator xsi:type="trl:SpoutCommands" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>LickSpoutStage.Commands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Trial</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Vision:PlayPenaltyFlash.bonsai">
              <Description>The penalty flash on DomeHardware's projector (lib-open-rigs PlayPenaltyFlash): each outcome TrialOutcomeEffects passes on whose PenaltyFlash plays (penalised, its kind's penalty.&lt;kind&gt;.flash.brightness above 0) flashes the whole field at that brightness at its rateHz for the penalty sound's length; TrialRules' PenaltyFlashes checked at Go against the sound.</Description>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="12" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="8" To="12" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="9" To="12" Label="Source4" />
            <Edge From="10" To="12" Label="Source5" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source6" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="43" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="26" To="27" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="28" To="29" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="30" To="31" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="32" To="33" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="33" To="34" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="34" To="35" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="36" To="37" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="37" To="38" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="38" To="39" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="40" To="41" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="41" To="42" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="39" To="44" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LabClockReady.bonsai">
        <Description>The lab clock checked at Start (OpenRigs.Logging LabClockReady): a clock that disagrees with the lab's stops the workflow before Ready; it announces LabClockChecked, which ReadyGate waits for (WorkflowStages).</Description>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:ExperimentRecords.bonsai">
        <Description>The controller's events (LogControlEvents), every Harp device in rig.yml checked at Start and recorded (RecordHarpDevices: the Behavior board, the timestamp generator, both stepper drivers and both Lickety Splits), and manifest.json (ExperimentManifest: the machine, this repo's commit, who launched it and sent Go, rig.yml and every file it names by hash ({RigFiles}: Projector-Mesh.csv, Projector-Gamma.bmp, the speakers' filters, the valve calibrations; the auditory stimuli are this repo's, in src\sounds, so the commit names them) and this mouse's spout positions, schemas\trial-columns.yml, and what the experiment must leave: a folder for each device in rig.yml, the Harp device records (harp), the three settings files and WorkflowData (Trials and Events), and in an optogenetics experiment Zapit's files: Camera-Zapit and the Zapit bank, sample, scanner fit and conditions settings, and with the laser enabled too (OptogeneticsLaserEnabled: rig.yml zapit.ceilingMw above 0) ZapitScanner and the accuracy settings, which only a beam makes). Last but LiveView, as it finds each device by the subjects published before it.</Description>
        <IngestScript>coen-dome-decision-making</IngestScript>
        <ExpectedFiles>auto;harp;Settings/Settings_Rig_;Settings/Settings_Task_;Settings/Settings_Combinations_;Settings/Settings_Experiment_;WorkflowData/WorkflowData_Trials_;WorkflowData/WorkflowData_Events_;Camera-Zapit/?Optogenetics;ZapitScanner/?OptogeneticsLaserEnabled;Settings/Settings_ZapitBank_?Optogenetics;Settings/Settings_ZapitSample_?Optogenetics;Settings/Settings_ZapitScannerFit_?Optogenetics;Settings/Settings_ZapitAccuracy_?OptogeneticsLaserEnabled;Settings/Settings_ZapitLaserCurve_?OptogeneticsLaserEnabled;Settings/Settings_ZapitConditions_?Optogenetics</ExpectedFiles>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every device in this machine's rig.yml that the workflow publishes, over ZeroMQ, for the live view (OpenRigs.LiveView): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558, from Start, in ready mode too. The three cameras as Camera-Face/Pupil/Body.video, 5 JPEG frames a second at 320 x 240, and the Behavior board's encoder from BehaviorBoard-Main.Data, 10 a second; each rate and size can be changed in rig.yml under the device's liveView:. Also elapsed, seconds since the experiment folder appeared, and liveview, this workflow and its commit. Every message carries the rig and the session key, ready until the experiment folder exists. Last in the workflow, because it streams only subjects built before it. A port already in use stops the workflow at Start.</Description>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="4" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
      <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
